From 792c0f088be0d16aeaeb322d5d20e081cd3c3275 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hejian Sang <sanghj0923@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:40:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Let jobs that share a TPU slice form their own process groups

Problem: PJRT needs WORLD_SIZE equal to the slice's device count, so every
process on a shared slice starts the runtime for the whole slice. After the
first (slice-sized) ProcessGroupTpu defines the world, every later group
gathers its membership across all slice processes and must partition the
slice, with a per-process gather counter. Two independent jobs on one slice
(e.g. an RL trainer on devices 0-3 and an inference engine on 4-7) must then
create every group in lockstep, and neither can init its own 4-rank
torch.distributed world.

Design (opt-in through TORCH_TPU_JOB_DEVICE_IDS, the comma-separated global
device ids of this job's processes in job-rank order):
- The first, slice-sized group still defines the world (rank-to-device map,
  topology order) and carries cross-job send/recv.
- A later group smaller than the slice is job-local: its layout is gathered
  among the job's processes only, in job-rank space, through the group's own
  store, then mapped back to world ranks. Its collectives compile on its own
  devices as before, and its global device assignment covers the job's
  layout, so programs mixing a job's groups still tile correctly. This
  covers the job's default group from init_process_group(world_size=4).
- Job-local gathers use their own counter and a key scope naming the job
  ("pg_sub:job<first id>:<n>:<rank>"), so the jobs' differing group counts
  do not shift the slice-wide gather ids and jobs sharing a root store do
  not collide. GatherSubgroupsViaNodeLocalStore takes the scope as a string;
  slice-wide keys are unchanged.
- The node-local store is off in job mode: it expects every device of the
  host to join each gather under one launcher.
- A group smaller than the slice that holds another job's processes fails
  the job-scoped partition check with an error naming the env var.

Unset env var: behavior is unchanged.

Limits: slice-sized groups other than the first (and collectives on the
slice group) still need every process of both jobs in the same order; a
job's layouts must partition the job, as layouts partition the world today;
size-1 groups keep the slice-wide layout; there is no public API to create
the slice group besides the tpu_dist backend constructor.

Tests: tests/distributed/job_local_process_group_test.py runs two 4-process
jobs on an 8-device v7x host with different group counts and orders,
collectives and a mixed compiled program inside each job, cross-job
send/recv and an all-reduce on the slice group. Error coverage baseline,
API baseline and docs updated. Not built or run yet.

